<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Puts the arachne's web trap in the hands of the tribe (user's call 2026-09-27: "give enemy
		arachnes the ability too").

		Vanilla does this by naming a concrete ability giver inside a think tree - Biotech does exactly
		this for the mech smokepop, a `JobGiver_AICastAbilityOnSelf` with `<ability>SmokepopMech</ability>`.
		Ours is a giver of our own, `PMM_Insects.JobGiver_WebTrapTarget`, because vanilla's
		`JobGiver_AICastAbility` is abstract and the only concrete one in the base game, `...OnSelf`, has
		nothing to do with throwing a web at somebody else. See Source/Insects/WebTrapAI.cs - the giver
		targets her current enemy and only fires for pawns hostile to the player, so a player's own
		arachne still waits to be told.

		Prepended to the root of the humanlike tree rather than appended: in a `ThinkNode_Priority` the
		first node that yields a job wins, and appending would park this behind the ordinary fight giver,
		which would mean she never webs at all. In front, she webs the moment she has an enemy in range
		and the ability is off cooldown - and while it recharges the base giver returns null and the fight
		giver below takes over, so she switches to her fists without any extra code.

		Gated on Alpha Animals: the think-tree node names `PMM_Ability_WebTrap`, and that ability def
		carries `MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals"`, so without AA this reference would dangle. Without AA
		the ability does not exist either, which is why the whole operation is behind the gate rather
		than the node carrying a `MayRequire` of its own - patch values are merged in after the loader
		has already resolved those attributes.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>Alpha Animals</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>Defs/ThinkTreeDef[defName="Humanlike"]/thinkRoot/subNodes</xpath>
			<order>Prepend</order>
			<value>
				<li Class="PMM_Insects.JobGiver_WebTrapTarget">
					<ability>PMM_Ability_WebTrap</ability>
				</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
